**Definition 6.1 (decoders).** Each decoder takes only its indicated
body, $b_*$ and PublicCode, with fresh work words. Each checks §5's
past predicates; its current caller has already performed the actual
current checks of Definition 5.1.

| Decoder | Actual finite word procedure |
| --- | --- |
| $D_S$ | Parse CYCLE masks and the exact unary layout; recover $W$; apply Definition 4.2; require $n=k$ and full derived raw endpoint equality; check binding and exact S re-encoding. |
| $D_B$ | Parse CYCLE contour, reconstruct terminal paths and their prefix closure, require maximality/exact contour re-encoding; invert layout; perform the same endpoint recovery/raw equality/binding checks and re-emit B. |
| $D_M$ | Parse exact seven-family schemas and canonical order; apply Definition 4.2 using basic families only; require $n=k$; fold roles over derived history and compare the entire reselected M-body; check binding. |
| $D_T$ | Start the paid foundation; for each eleven-field record take its own optional bit exactly at IN, execute one literal Step and local patch check, compare every record field, update identities/roles/tally; require exhaustion and $k$, then binding and exact T re-encoding. |

Reject IN with no bit, non-IN with a supplied bit, a mismatch or a
noncanonical body. Each successful decoder can emit the RCA/ARC
HistoricalImage value of its derived prefix, including its redundant
semantic fold. No decoder reads firstS, the saved initial Image,
another view, a stored package input or family5 to reconstruct input.

